                <note rend="inline" type="source">861a.01/228: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Warren</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-04-08T10:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 8,
                                1922—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 8—8:50
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>59. Following from Vladivostok dated April 5, 11 a.m.</p>
                <p>“There are unofficial reports that battle at Spassk was on larger scale than the
                    Japanese have indicated and that losses on both sides were heavy. Monday and
                    Tuesday the Japanese sent 99 troop cars, that is, about 2,500 men, from Nikolsk
                    to Spassk. Today they are sending 64 troop cars from Vladivostok to
                    Nikolsk.[”]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Warren</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
